e.out on both standbys; their creation served evidence collection, but the files were not cleaned up. No failed services or package damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4ecc97c212994132","cmd-98d872b608394c73","cmd-67615a16f8a643e7","cmd-ee722b0b1c2c4e26","cmd-6794ca7f42cb4b60","cmd-5ae8b0dc0b944f7c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete for every node: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, recovered PostgreSQL/data/cluster state, and a fresh transaction replicated after all restarts. Lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor's observations.","limitations":["There was no separate in-guest management interface on which to perform a negative PostgreSQL connection probe; network isolation is established by topology/interface inventories and address-specific listeners.","The lifecycle collector inventories temporary filenames but not their contents or sizes; the retained diagnostic files are therefore assessed from the commands that created them."]}
